      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pregnancy in patients with severe hypercholesterolemia and coronary artery disease results in multiple problems both for mother and fetus; the most potent agents for low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol reduction, the HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors (statins) cannot be used during pregnancy. We present a case in which LDL apheresis via heparin-induced extracorporeal LDL precipitation was employed safely and efficaciously during pregnancy in a woman with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia and stable coronary artery disease."},
